                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#4e79a7' fontsize='24'>Formula 1 Performance &amp; Reliability Dashboard</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#4e79a7' fontsize='20'>2020 – 2024</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='5135' id='7' type-v2='text' w='98770' x='615' y='4154'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='15'>This dashboard provides a clear and unbiased overview of driver and constructor performance across five Formula 1 seasons, from 2020 to 2024. It focuses on the most important measurable outcomes: points scored, race wins, podium  finishes, and reliability. </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='15'>By combining championship results with retirement data, the dashboard helps explain not only who performed best, but also which teams and drivers lost valuable points due to mechanical failures or accidents.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
